      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T13:54:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When we call `setTemplate` for appending instance data, the `vertices` is the BindBufferInfo associated with that RenderStep\u0027s static vertex data.  To benefit from the stride aligning this change adds, we need to detect that `vertices`\u0027s offset is a multiple of the vertex stride and updating pendingBaseVertex and set `vertices` to be at offset 0.  But we would also need to compare whether or not the prior pending base vertex was different and trigger a flush.\n\nWith the way it\u0027s currently written, I think we end up with essentially the same binding commands as before, with the benefit of explicitly representing the base instances and base vertices separately.\n\nGiven the complexities of keeping these pending base parameters in sync with the bindings, I\u0027m more and more leaning to landing this CL without further changes to setTemplate (so we aren\u0027t really changing binding behavior yet), and then update `DrawWriter` to track bound BindBufferInfos and pending BindBufferInfos explicitly so that flushing in setTemplate() is simply checking the old pending BBIs with the new BBIs, and then in `flush()` we convert pending BBIs to a canonical BBI @ offset 0 with a pendingBase before comparing with the bound BBIs to issue new commands.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "e8e4310685db3aae7f99c355ac0ad3b2ec969069",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
